It is an original superred SecurityClaim port of the NVIDIA Aegis AI Content
Safety benchmark. The safety judge is our own scoring choice (see ASSUMPTIONS.md);
it is NOT NVIDIA's Aegis-Guard classifier.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Benchmark dataset (VENDORED, CC-BY-4.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source : NVIDIA Aegis AI Content Safety Dataset 1.0 (a.k.a. Nemotron Content
         Safety Dataset V1),
         https://huggingface.co/datasets/nvidia/Aegis-AI-Content-Safety-Dataset-1.0
License: CC-BY-4.0 (full text in LICENSES/aegis-dataset-CC-BY-4.0.txt)
Curated by: Shaona Ghosh, NVIDIA.
Pinned revision: bd96d862068e47630197de64eb91f8d1481ff3e0 (test split)
Files  : src/aegis_claim/_vendor/Content Moderation Extracted Annotations
         02.08.24_test_release_0418_v1.parquet   (byte-identical upstream parquet)
         src/aegis_claim/_vendor/aegis_test.csv   (deterministic CSV rendering)

The dataset is redistributed here under CC-BY-4.0 with attribution. It is
vendored byte-identically (parquet) plus a deterministic CSV rendering, both
sha256-pinned in _vendor/SHA256SUMS and checked against the pinned revision by
scripts/sync_upstream.py --check. NO CHANGES were made to the parquet; the CSV is
a lossless column-for-column rendering of it. The claim uses only the unsafe
user-message prompts and records each row's Aegis risk category.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Taxonomy and methodology
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Paper  : Shaona Ghosh, Prasoon Varshney, Erick Galinkin, Christopher Parisien,
         "AEGIS: Online Adaptive AI Content Safety Moderation with Ensemble of
         LLM Experts", arXiv:2404.05993 (NVIDIA).

The 13 Aegis harm-category names reproduced in src/aegis_claim/categories.py are
taken from the dataset's own labels; the taxonomy is described in the paper and
dataset card.

